Chapter: Modbus

 Modbus fieldbus protocol per the Modbus Application Protocol v1.1b3
 and Modbus over Serial Line v1.02. The industrial workhorse for
 talking to PLCs, meters, and sensors over RS485/RS232 (Modbus RTU)
 or TCP (Modbus TCP). Each builder returns a List Integer (the raw
 bytes). Transport is handled by the caller: a serial UART for RTU,
 a TCP socket for TCP.

 A Modbus message is a PDU (function code plus data). RTU wraps the
 PDU with a unit address and a trailing CRC-16. TCP wraps the PDU
 with a 7-byte MBAP header and no checksum (TCP already protects the
 payload).

Section: Function Codes

  modbus-fc-read-coils : Integer = 1
  modbus-fc-read-discrete-inputs : Integer = 2
  modbus-fc-read-holding-registers : Integer = 3
  modbus-fc-read-input-registers : Integer = 4
  modbus-fc-write-single-coil : Integer = 5
  modbus-fc-write-single-register : Integer = 6
  modbus-fc-write-multiple-coils : Integer = 15
  modbus-fc-write-multiple-registers : Integer = 16
  modbus-fc-read-exception-status : Integer = 7
  modbus-fc-diagnostics : Integer = 8
  modbus-fc-mask-write-register : Integer = 22
  modbus-fc-read-write-multiple-registers : Integer = 23

Section: Exception Codes

 Exception responses set the high bit of the function code (fc + 128)
 and carry a one-byte exception code.

  modbus-ex-illegal-function : Integer = 1
  modbus-ex-illegal-data-address : Integer = 2
  modbus-ex-illegal-data-value : Integer = 3
  modbus-ex-server-device-failure : Integer = 4

Section: Byte Helpers

 A 16-bit value is transmitted big-endian on the wire (high byte
 first) inside every PDU field.

  modbus-u16 : Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-u16 (v) = [bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255, bit-and v 255]

Section: CRC-16

 CRC-16/Modbus: reflected polynomial 0xA001, initial value 0xFFFF,
 no final xor. The RTU frame appends the CRC low byte first, then
 the high byte. Running the CRC over a complete frame including its
 own trailing CRC yields zero, which is how a receiver validates a
 frame.

  modbus-crc16 : List Integer -> Integer
  modbus-crc16 (bs) = modbus-crc16-update #FFFF bs 0 (list-length bs)

  modbus-crc16-update : Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  modbus-crc16-update (crc) (bs) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then crc
   else modbus-crc16-update (modbus-crc16-byte (bit-xor crc (list-at bs i)) 0) bs (i + 1) len

  modbus-crc16-byte : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  modbus-crc16-byte (crc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then crc
   else if bit-and crc 1 == 1
     then modbus-crc16-byte (bit-xor (bit-shru crc 1) #A001) (k + 1)
     else modbus-crc16-byte (bit-shru crc 1) (k + 1)

Section: Read Request PDUs

 The four read functions share a shape: function code, starting
 address (2 bytes), and quantity (2 bytes).

  modbus-read-coils : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-read-coils (start) (qty) =
   [modbus-fc-read-coils] & modbus-u16 start & modbus-u16 qty

  modbus-read-discrete-inputs : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-read-discrete-inputs (start) (qty) =
   [modbus-fc-read-discrete-inputs] & modbus-u16 start & modbus-u16 qty

  modbus-read-holding-registers : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-read-holding-registers (start) (qty) =
   [modbus-fc-read-holding-registers] & modbus-u16 start & modbus-u16 qty

  modbus-read-input-registers : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-read-input-registers (start) (qty) =
   [modbus-fc-read-input-registers] & modbus-u16 start & modbus-u16 qty

Section: Write Request PDUs

 Write single coil encodes the on state as 0xFF00 and off as 0x0000.

  modbus-write-single-coil : Integer, Boolean -> List Integer
  modbus-write-single-coil (addr) (on) =
   [modbus-fc-write-single-coil] & modbus-u16 addr & modbus-u16 (if on then #FF00 else 0)

  modbus-write-single-register : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-write-single-register (addr) (value) =
   [modbus-fc-write-single-register] & modbus-u16 addr & modbus-u16 value

  modbus-write-multiple-registers : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-write-multiple-registers (start) (values) =
   let qty = list-length values
   in let byte-count = qty * 2
   in [modbus-fc-write-multiple-registers] & modbus-u16 start & modbus-u16 qty & [byte-count] & modbus-encode-registers values 0 qty []

  modbus-encode-registers : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-encode-registers (values) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else modbus-encode-registers values (i + 1) len (acc & modbus-u16 (list-at values i))

 Write multiple coils packs the coil states into bytes, LSB first:
 coil 0 is bit 0 of the first data byte. The byte count is the
 quantity of coils rounded up to a whole number of bytes.

  modbus-write-multiple-coils : Integer, List Boolean -> List Integer
  modbus-write-multiple-coils (start) (coils) =
   let qty = list-length coils
   in let byte-count = bit-shru (qty + 7) 3
   in [modbus-fc-write-multiple-coils] & modbus-u16 start & modbus-u16 qty & [byte-count] & modbus-pack-coils coils 0 byte-count []

  modbus-pack-coils : List Boolean, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-pack-coils (coils) (b) (byte-count) (acc) =
   if b >= byte-count then acc
   else modbus-pack-coils coils (b + 1) byte-count (list-push acc (modbus-pack-byte coils (b * 8) 0 0 (list-length coils)))

  modbus-pack-byte : List Boolean, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  modbus-pack-byte (coils) (base) (bit) (acc) (qty) =
   if bit >= 8 then acc
   else let idx = base + bit
   in let set = if idx >= qty then 0 else if list-at coils idx then bit-shl 1 bit else 0
   in modbus-pack-byte coils base (bit + 1) (bit-or acc set) qty

Section: Diagnostic and Combined PDUs

 Read Exception Status has no data. Mask Write Register applies an AND
 mask then an OR mask to a holding register. Read/Write Multiple
 Registers reads one block and writes another in a single transaction.

  modbus-read-exception-status : List Integer
  modbus-read-exception-status = [modbus-fc-read-exception-status]

  modbus-mask-write-register : Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-mask-write-register (addr) (and-mask) (or-mask) =
   [modbus-fc-mask-write-register] & modbus-u16 addr & modbus-u16 and-mask & modbus-u16 or-mask

  modbus-read-write-multiple-registers : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-read-write-multiple-registers (read-start) (read-qty) (write-start) (write-values) =
   let qty = list-length write-values
   in [modbus-fc-read-write-multiple-registers] & modbus-u16 read-start & modbus-u16 read-qty & modbus-u16 write-start & modbus-u16 qty & [qty * 2] & modbus-encode-registers write-values 0 qty []

Section: RTU Framing

 Modbus RTU: unit address, PDU, then CRC-16 (low byte first).

  modbus-rtu-frame : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-rtu-frame (unit-id) (pdu) =
   let body = [unit-id] & pdu
   in let crc = modbus-crc16 body
   in body & [bit-and crc 255, bit-and (bit-shru crc 8) 255]

  modbus-rtu-check : List Integer -> Boolean
  modbus-rtu-check (frame) = modbus-crc16 frame == 0

Section: ASCII Framing

 Modbus ASCII: a colon, then the unit address, PDU, and LRC rendered as
 uppercase ASCII hex, then CR LF. The LRC is the two's complement of the
 sum of the binary bytes (address plus PDU).

  modbus-sum : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  modbus-sum (bytes) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else modbus-sum bytes (i + 1) len (acc + list-at bytes i)

  modbus-lrc : List Integer -> Integer
  modbus-lrc (bytes) = bit-and (256 - bit-and (modbus-sum bytes 0 (list-length bytes) 0) 255) 255

  modbus-ascii-nibble : Integer -> Integer
  modbus-ascii-nibble (n) = if n < 10 then n + 48 else n + 55

  modbus-ascii-hex-byte : Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-ascii-hex-byte (b) = [modbus-ascii-nibble (bit-shru b 4), modbus-ascii-nibble (bit-and b 15)]

  modbus-ascii-hex : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-ascii-hex (bytes) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else modbus-ascii-hex bytes (i + 1) len (acc & modbus-ascii-hex-byte (list-at bytes i))

  modbus-ascii-frame : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-ascii-frame (unit-id) (pdu) =
   let content = [unit-id] & pdu
   in let full = content & [modbus-lrc content]
   in [#3A] & modbus-ascii-hex full 0 (list-length full) [] & [#0D, #0A]

Section: TCP Framing

 Modbus TCP wraps the PDU in a 7-byte MBAP header: transaction id
 (2), protocol id (2, always zero), length (2, counting the unit id
 and PDU), and unit id (1). No CRC.

  modbus-tcp-frame : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-tcp-frame (txn) (unit-id) (pdu) =
   let length = list-length pdu + 1
   in modbus-u16 txn & [0, 0] & modbus-u16 length & [unit-id] & pdu

Section: Response Parsing

 A read-registers response is function code, byte count, then the
 register values big-endian. Parse them into a List Integer of
 16-bit values.

  modbus-parse-registers : List Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-parse-registers (pdu) =
   let count = list-at pdu 1
   in modbus-parse-registers-loop pdu 2 (2 + count) []

  modbus-parse-registers-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-parse-registers-loop (pdu) (i) (stop) (acc) =
   if i >= stop then acc
   else modbus-parse-registers-loop pdu (i + 2) stop (list-push acc (bit-or (bit-shl (list-at pdu i) 8) (list-at pdu (i + 1))))

 A read-coils response is function code, byte count, then packed
 coil bits (LSB first). Unpack the requested quantity into booleans.

  modbus-parse-coils : List Integer, Integer -> List Boolean
  modbus-parse-coils (pdu) (quantity) = modbus-parse-coils-loop pdu quantity 0 []

  modbus-parse-coils-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Boolean -> List Boolean
  modbus-parse-coils-loop (pdu) (quantity) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= quantity then acc
   else modbus-parse-coils-loop pdu quantity (i + 1) (list-push acc (bit-and (bit-shru (list-at pdu (2 + bit-shru i 3)) (bit-and i 7)) 1 == 1))

  modbus-is-exception : List Integer -> Boolean
  modbus-is-exception (pdu) = list-at pdu 0 >= 128

  modbus-exception-code : List Integer -> Integer
  modbus-exception-code (pdu) = list-at pdu 1

  modbus-exception-pdu : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  modbus-exception-pdu (fc) (code) = [bit-or fc 128, code]
